{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795538376,"nonce":"P5hT+M0XQe/1SixFJapjtQarUi0=","title":"Fresh-resolve job passes while its yanked-release check never runs","message":"The scheduled Fresh resolve workflow copies ci/workspace.lock to Cargo.lock and runs `cargo fetch --locked 2\u003e\u00261 | tee fetch.log`, then fails only if fetch.log mentions \"yanked\". On run 45227896091 (2026-11-23, at 908d5dae) the fetch stopped at once: \"cannot update the lock file ... because --locked was passed to prevent this\". The pipe's status is tee's, so the step passed, and no download happened that could report a yanked release.\n\nWhy the lock needs updating: ci/workspace.lock was last written in 5e354d22 (2026-11-06) and has no entries for crates added since, accesskit among them. Since 975c2d07 the root manifest also patches wgpu-hal to third_party/wgpu-hal, which changes that entry from a registry source to a path.\n\nFix: run scripts/ci-refresh-lock.sh and commit the lock after a build and test pass, and make the step fail on fetch's own status (`set -o pipefail`, or check `${PIPESTATUS[0]}`), so a stale lock fails the job instead of passing it.","files":null}]}